Describe a time when you missed or were late for a meeting
- when it happened
- what happened
- when you missed/were late for it
- explain how you felt about this experience

One memorable time when I was late for a meeting was during my first year at university. It was an important group meeting for a project presentation, and we had arranged to meet in the library early in the morning.

The night before, I stayed up really late studying for another exam, so I was completely exhausted. I planned to wake up early and even set an alarm, but somehow I slept through it. When I finally woke up, I realized the meeting had already started almost an hour earlier.

I panicked immediately because I knew my teammates were relying on me. I quickly called them to apologize and told them I was on my way. Then I rushed out of my dorm without even having breakfast.

When I arrived, everyone was already discussing the final part of the project, so I had missed a lot of important information. My teammates were a bit annoyed, which I completely understood. I felt really guilty for wasting their time and not being responsible enough.

After that experience, I learned a valuable lesson about punctuality and time management. Since then, I’ve tried to organize my schedule better and avoid staying up too late before important events. I also learned that good communication is essential when working in a team.
